<title>SWITZERLAND: ACI says Anchorage top world cargo airport in June.</title>
<headline>ACI says Anchorage top world cargo airport in June.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anchorage was the world's busiest cargo airport in June 1996, compared to the same month last year, said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI).</p>
<p>The airport handled 199,981 tonnes of cargo up 149.7 percent on June 1995. This is the first time that Anchorage has topped the airport rankings since ACI records started in 1992.</p>
<p>Occupying second-place in the ACI table of top cargo-handling airports was Memphis, base of U.S. express freight carrier, Federal Express, as a result of reporting 167,816 tonnes, up 15.2 percent on the previous year's levels.</p>
<p>In third place was Los Angeles airport which handled 145,022 tonnes, an increase of 13.7 percent on June 1995.</p>
<p>The world's 20 busiest cargo airports in June 1996, with the volume they handled, the percentage change over June 1995 and, in parentheses, their June 1995 ranking, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  (14) Anchorage	 199,981 tonnes  (up 149.7pct)</p>
<p> 2  (1)  Memphis	   167,816 tonnes  (up  15.2)</p>
<p> 3  (4)  Los Angeles     145,022 tonnes  (up  13.7)</p>
<p> 4  (3)  New York	  138,442 tonnes  (up   7.6)</p>
<p> 5  (2)  Tokyo	     133,355 tonnes  (down 8.7)</p>
<p> 6  (5)  Miami	     133,350 tonnes  (up   7.7)</p>
<p> 7  (3)  Hong Kong	 127,042 tonnes  (up   5.1)</p>
<p> 8  (7)  Frankfurt	 122,132 tonnes  (up   2.7)</p>
<p> 9  (8)  Louisville	112,109 tonnes  (down 3.3)</p>
<p> 10 (12) Chicago	   108,962 tonnes  (up  22.1)</p>
<p> 11 (9)  Seoul	     108,770 tonnes  (up  11.5)</p>
<p> 12 (10) Singapore	  99,443 tonnes  (up   3.2)</p>
<p> 13 (11) London Heathrow  97,911 tonnes  (up   2.6)</p>
<p> 14 (13) Amsterdam	  88,157 tonnes  (up   9.0)</p>
<p> 15 (15) Paris-CDG	  83,242 tonnes  (up   5.6)</p>
<p> 16 (16) New York Newark  80,942 tonnes  (up   2.7)</p>
<p> 17 (-)  Dayton	     65,463 tonnes  (up  28.9)</p>
<p> 18 (18) Taipei	     65,345 tonnes  (up   2.3)</p>
<p> 19 (19) Atlanta	    65,325 tonnes  (up   7.1)</p>
<p> 20 (17) Dallas F/Worth   62,970 tonnes  (down 1.5)</p>
